<ServiceLayout title="Freelance UX & Design Support for Agencies" description="Senior freelance UX strategy and product design for agency client projects. Work directly with Angelo Manzano Jr. on discovery, interfaces and design systems." label="ChrowmDesigns / For agencies" heading="A senior design partner for your next client project." intro="When your agency needs experienced UX and product design support, I can join the project with a defined role and a clear scope. Work directly with Angelo Manzano Jr., from the first conversation through design delivery.">
  <section class="service-section" aria-labelledby="agency-support"><h2 id="agency-support">Bring me in where the work needs it.</h2><div class="service-grid">
    <div><h3>Shape the direction</h3><p>Get support with discovery, experience reviews, information architecture, and user flows. Useful when a client brief needs to become a clear design plan before production begins.</p></div>
    <div><h3>Move the design forward</h3><p>Add senior design capacity for a website, digital product, or campaign experience. The engagement can cover wireframes, responsive interfaces, and interactive prototypes.</p></div>
    <div><h3>Connect the system</h3><p>Bring consistency to a growing set of screens and components. I can work within an existing visual direction or help define reusable patterns for the project.</p></div>
    <div><h3>Support the handoff</h3><p>Help your team communicate design intent through interface states, component guidance, and implementation discussions. We agree on the handoff and support required as part of the scope.</p></div>
  </div><a href="/services/">Explore the design services ↗</a></section>
  <section class="service-section" aria-labelledby="agency-process"><h2 id="agency-process">A clear working arrangement</h2><ol>
    <li><strong>Share the brief.</strong> Send the client challenge, project stage, expected timeline, and the role you need filled.</li>
    <li><strong>Agree on the scope.</strong> We define deliverables, responsibilities, review points, budget, and availability before work begins.</li>
    <li><strong>Work with your team.</strong> We establish how design decisions, feedback, and client communication will be handled.</li>
    <li><strong>Hand over with context.</strong> Your team receives the agreed design files and guidance needed for the next stage.</li>
  </ol></section>
  <section class="service-section" aria-labelledby="agency-work"><h2 id="agency-work">Selected work across complex brands</h2><p>Explore the project context and my contribution in each case study.</p><div class="service-grid">
    <div class="service-proof"><a class="service-proof__image-link" href="/cases/malibu-rum/" aria-label="View case study: Malibu Rum campaign design"><img src="/images/malibu-case_thumb.webp" alt="Malibu Rum campaign design" width="760" height="520" loading="lazy" /></a><h3>Malibu Rum</h3><p>Creative systems and campaign design across a multi-agency project.</p><a href="/cases/malibu-rum/">Explore the Malibu Rum case study ↗</a></div>
    <div class="service-proof"><a class="service-proof__image-link" href="/cases/beat-saber/" aria-label="View case study: Beat Saber Music Pack visual design"><img src="/images/beat_saber-case_thumb.webp" alt="Beat Saber Music Pack visual design" width="760" height="520" loading="lazy" /></a><h3>Beat Saber</h3><p>Brand expression and creative systems for a digital entertainment experience.</p><a href="/cases/beat-saber/">Explore the Beat Saber case study ↗</a></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="service-section" aria-labelledby="agency-questions"><h2 id="agency-questions">Before we start</h2>
    <details><summary>Can we bring you into an existing project?</summary><p>Yes. Share the current designs, constraints, and the gap you need covered. We can identify a focused role and agree on how I’ll work with your team.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Do you work with agencies outside Florida?</summary><p>Yes. I’m based in Palm Bay, Florida, and work remotely with agencies and teams nationwide. Meeting schedules and collaboration expectations are agreed at the start.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What should we send for an estimate?</summary><p>A short brief, the expected deliverables, your target dates, and an indication of budget. If those are still taking shape, tell me what is known and what needs defining.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How are client communication and confidentiality handled?</summary><p>We discuss your agency’s requirements before the engagement and agree on communication, access, confidentiality, and how the work may be credited or shared.</p></details>
  </section>
  <section class="service-section"><h2>Have a project in mind?</h2><p>Tell me what your team is taking on and where you need support. I’ll help you assess scope and fit.</p><a href="/contact/">Discuss your agency project ↗</a></section>
</ServiceLayout>
